## 1. What is a cookie?

A cookie is a small file saved by your browser. This site also uses the browser’s “local storage”, which works the same way. On this page, we call both “cookies”.

## 2. What this site uses today

{% without-consent %}
Only what is needed for the site to work. No advertising cookies, no audience measurement for now.
{% /without-consent %}

{% with-consent %}
What is needed for the site to work and, only with your consent, the cookies marked “With your consent”.
{% /with-consent %}

{% storage-table /%}

## 3. Cookies that need your consent

{% with-consent %}
Audience measurement (knowing which pages are read) and partner links (letting brands know that you come from this site). They are never set without your consent. Your choice is kept for 6 months, then we ask you again.
{% /with-consent %}

{% without-consent %}
Today, the site uses none. If this changes, a banner will ask for your consent first.
{% /without-consent %}

## 4. Changing your mind

{% with-consent %}
You can change your choice at any time:

{% cookie-settings /%}

You can also delete cookies in your browser settings.
{% /with-consent %}

{% without-consent %}
You can delete cookies at any time in your browser settings.
{% /without-consent %}

## 5. Videos

The site’s videos are hosted on this site: they do not set cookies.

